     Homer saw it as the Ocean Stream that flowed around the earth,
while many cultures claimed it for their own geographical rivers, such as
the Rhine of Europe and the Ebro of Spain. Richard Allen points out,
however, that really only the Nile could lay claim to mirroring this starry
river because that river flows from north to south, as does Eridanus.—
