square/golden Mean was used by the Celts who built Newgrange1^ to
signify a year. The actual symbol of a square or rectangle signified that
the group had knowledge of the year and was proudly chiseled in stone
over the lightbox at Newgrange. By the time of the ingress of the
equinox into Aries, the developing monotheistic religions built their
