circles the North Pole, the pivot point of the world, the point of stillness.
Here was the source of life itself, and next to this sacred point was
placed the great She-Bear goddess. Her first appearance in written
history is in the Babylonian creation myth but by that stage she was

already ancient.— In India the seven stars of Ursa Major were called the
Seven Bears and in North America, long before the arrival of the white
race, the constellation was known as Paukuuawa or Okuari, both words
meaning "bear" in the languages of tribes of the Blackfeet and the

Iroquois.—
