PHACT: THE CONCEPT

           It is obvious that Robson, Ebertin, and Rigor are drawing on the
   symbolism of the dove to derive their meanings of artistic talents and
   harmony. But this star used to be part of the Argo on the top of the bow,
   crashing through the waves in waters uncharted. The symbolism here
   should not be the seventeenth century peaceful dove but rather the
   ancient quest for adventure. Carl Jung had Phact rising as his Moon
