VISIBLE HELIACAL RISING

        Another 10 days or so, and the Sun will be at 20° Leo. Sirius will
   rise before the Sun, co-rising with 9° Leo, and set before the Sun sets.
   However, Sirius will be visible in the early morning sky for a short
   period before sunrise. This is known as the visible heliacal rising phase,
   also called the apparent heliacal rising phase for Sirius, which marks the
   visible end to the period of arising and lying hidden (see figure 27. p.
   324).
